 with fewer honors, possibly aiming for All Simples or a suit-focused hand.  \n\nReason: F2 is a single honor with low probability of completing a pung, and it doesn\u2019t contribute to sequences. Removing it early streamlines your hand toward more feasible patterns like Mixed Straight or Half Flush (using W and J2).  \n\nAnswer: Play F2"}
