irs? But I have J2 pung already so not Seven Pairs.  \nIf keep B3 B4, can chow with B2/B5 but B2 has 4 left, B5 has 1 left \u2014 not great.  \n\nBetter to aim for W-based hand: W3 W4 could become chow with W5 (draw W5) and maybe another W pair.  \n\nSo discard B9 now is safe and doesn\u2019t break much potential.  \n\n**Reason:**  \nB9 is relatively safe (3 left), and discarding it now doesn\u2019t hurt hand\u2019s flexibility toward a W + honors hand. F1 is riskier given only 1 left unseen and might give someone a needed honor for all honors hand. Other tiles like W3/W4 could become chow material; T3 is a good pair; B3/B4 also could form sequences but less likely since B5 is scarce.  \n\n**Answer:** Play B9"}
